WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.640
[Music]

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.640
[Narrator:] This is the story of an opportunity 
offered to the daughters of the Navajo, Cherokee,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:32.680
Choctaw, Seneca, to the Pueblo people, the Sioux, 
Winnebago, Apache, to all the Indian peoples.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:44.680
[Music

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.200
The story of an unusual school.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:57.620
Each year 80 young Indian girls enroll in the 
practical nurse school in Albuquerque.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.680
They come to build a career for themselves and to 
learn to serve the cause of health

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.480
among their people.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.880
They come from many tribes and many parts of the 
country.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.940
From Oklahoma, Lita Mae Gumbai.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.880
[Lita Mae Gumbai:] When they told me at Haskell Institute about the practical nursing school,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.900
I really wanted to go.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.980
My parents were so pleased.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.000
[Narrator:] Norma Marie Ahiti.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.160
[Norma Marie Ahiti:] I am smiling here in this picture taken at the school, but I was a little frightened,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.880
I think, when packing to come.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.680
[Narrator:] From New Mexico, Elsie Curlee.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.880
[Elsie Curlee:] Our high school guidance teacher 
told us about the school.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.840
[Narrator:] Harriet St. Clair's mother is a practical 
nurse.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.520
Lois Bohannon had two sisters at the practical 
nurse school before her.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.360
Three cousins came together from Laguna.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.440
[Della Davis:] Della Davis.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.480
[Isabel Gaistein:] Isabel Gaistein.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.200
[Violet Sophski:] Violet Sophski.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.360
[Narrator:] Laverna Cucka of Arizona had always wanted to be a nurse,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.800
and so had Rose Gomez of Taos.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.000
[Rose Gomez:] I saw the good care the nurses 
gave in the hospital.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:11.120
It made me want to help people that way too, 
especially the children.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.200
[Narrator:] Nancy Cohawk came from Minnesota.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.080
Laverna High Hawk and Georgia Anne Eagle came 
from South Dakota.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:25.560
Janice Armstrong came the greatest distance, all 
the way from New York State.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.040
Classes begin at the school in August and 
February each year.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.320
Many students are brought by their family.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.000
Others come by train.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.040
Joe Hueron meets them with the school car.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.720
On arrival, Lita Mae Gumbai and Harriet St. Clair stop to look at the school sign.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.760
They didn't quite know what to expect.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.000
The first day was a busy one.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.160
There were roommates to get acquainted with.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:55.720
Lita Mae meets hers, Cecelia Mirabal from Taos.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:04.840
With unpacking to do, getting settled, receiving uniforms, trying them on for the first time.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.000
There were the teachers to meet, the school to see,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.760
and that night a letter to write home.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.960
[Lita Mae Gumbai:] Dear Mother, our school being next door to the Indian boarding school,

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.160
there isn't time to be homesick.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.880
It is a big and friendly campus.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.520
A church is just across the street.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.240
We have a cat here named Professor.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:38.680
[Narrator:] There is a great deal to learn, to do, to 
think about and understand.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:44.960
Anatomy, the organs of the body, and the bones of the body.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:51.400
The patient's skeleton here surrounded is Oscar 
Gerard Albuquerque, a favorite of the girls.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.640
The words are difficult as Miss Mirabal discovers.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:01.760
Students learn how to make hospital beds, how to read a thermometer, and take temperatures,

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.520
pulse, and respiration.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:10.280
They learn about diets and how to serve food to 
bed patients.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:13.160
How to take blood pressures.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:19.720
The combined class and demonstration room lets 
some students watch while others practice.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.280
Sometimes on each other,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:27.280
as here with Lita Mae, learning how to get a patient out of bed and into a wheelchair.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.960
Sometimes they practice with dolls.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.760
They call them Mr. and Mrs. Chase, for the 
manufacturer who makes them.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:42.000
Students also go to the Albuquerque sanatorium 
for a first look at what is ahead.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.400
Here, their pink uniforms are covered with a 
protective hospital gown, and they wear masks

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.080
over nose and mouth.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:57.960
Time now to use what they have learned for real people, really ill, to feel needed and appreciated.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:04.160
Back in classes at the school, questions are sometimes easy,

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.560
and everyone knows the answers.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:14.160
Sometimes not so easy, and no one knows, but 
there are teachers and books to help.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.920
It isn't all work, of course.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.400
The chuckwagon is a popular interruption to classes.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.240
Twice a day everyone flocks outside.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:31.280
There's plenty of time for play, picnics and 
cookouts, hotdogs and watermelon.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:38.760
Regular meals are taken across the campus in the 
big cafeteria with the boarding school students.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.120
Sports are popular after class.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.880
Strenuous tennis.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.720
Less strenuous croquet.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.360
Archery is a favorite, naturally.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.520
Pull.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.720
Bull's-eye. Twice.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.280
There's time for dancing with each other on the 
school porch and for dancing with their dates,

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.040
perhaps from the boarding school.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.440
Teas and parties are learning time as well as fun.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.520
How to set the table, how to serve, and to meet guests.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.960
Here one of the doctors is a guest.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:19.120
Cards are played some free evenings, and music others.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.560
Television in the upstairs living room is a favorite.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.240
And getting to know each other is probably best of 
all.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.680
Exchanging confidences,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.120
showing pictures in each other's rooms at night,

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.760
getting to know all about each other.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.120
[Lita Mae Gumbai:] Some of us who are city girls 
had never seen a reservation.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.880
Elsie Curlee showed me what a hogan is like.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.880
Now I am anxious to visit one.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.960
[Speaker 1:] I showed some of my Navajo paintings 
too.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.840
They liked them.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.120
They're beautiful.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.560
[Girls:] How pretty!

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:54.400
[Speaker 2:] This is the way my people paint.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.960
Apache art shows much action.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.160
[Laverna Cucka:] The Hopis are the ones who make Kachina dolls.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.280
See, this is a mudhead, one of our clowns.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.840
[Speaker 3:] Do you like the pottery we make, in 
our pueblo?

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.160
[Girls:] Very much. Very much.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.840
[Speaker 3:] My grandmother Maria made this.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.240
[Narrator:] Other arts are exhibited also.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:24.280
Miss Curlee shows how to make fry bread, and boyfriends and dates are discussed.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.640
They chatter and giggle and have a fine time.

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:30.480
They become fast friends.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:39.040
On Saturdays they go shopping, and to church on Sundays.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.960
Letters home now are full of news.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:50.600
[Lita Mae Gumbai:] Albuquerque is a busy city with busy streets, but it has quiet places, too.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.100
The state university is here.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:59.320
At sundown, Sandia Mountains to the east turn as pink as our uniforms.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.720
[Narrator:] The storied Santa Fe is nearby.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.440
The girls have opportunities to visit.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.960
Graduate practical nurses serve at the Indian 
hospital at Santa Fe.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:16.760
Many of the most famous southwestern pueblos are only a few hours from Albuquerque:

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:22.800
Taos, San Ildefonso, home of the famous black pottery,

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.720
old Santa Ana,

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.120
Zuni, noted for its silversmiths

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.920
and its waffle gardens,

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:37.440
old Acoma in the sky, Ariabe.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.480
Many of these are home to some of the students, 
and they delight in showing them to their friends

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.320
who come from far away.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.400
This is fabulous country, truly.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:57.400
The land of the seven cities of Cibola, the ancient civilizations, and the wonders of nature.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:10.040
Gallup, where the inter-tribal ceremonials are held 
each July, is only half a day away.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:18.040
So many things to see, but after the weekend's sightseeing and fun,

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:23.320
back to books and classrooms, for examinations will be coming soon.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:28.440
Names and grades are posted, and the girls crowd 
around to look for their marks.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.760
At the end of four months, the successful students receive their caps.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.680
Probation is over.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:43.960
Now, indeed, there is news to write home, for Lita Mae, Norma Marie, Rose Gomez,

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:50.360
and the others will leave the school for a while to go out for clinical and public health experience,

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.000
working under supervision of registered nurses in the Indian Health Program.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.840
Some will go to the Albuquerque sanatorium, 
already familiar.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.640
Others, the majority, will go to the Navajo 
reservation.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.600
Here they will serve the seven months at the 
Navajo Medical Center.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.480
They will live in the nurses' home.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:23.440
They have their own counselor and teacher, for 
here also they go to school,

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.240
but there is a difference.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:30.360
They study now the care and problems affecting 
actual individual patients.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:33.200
No longer practice. This is real.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:36.760
Each has certain patients of her own to care for.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.080
The elderly,

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:43.360
the newborn--a favorite assignment--

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.960
mother and baby together,

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:49.600
the restless youngsters in pediatrics.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:53.880
Small problems sometimes present themselves.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:58.840
[Lita Mae Gumbai:] The first time I was to give bed baths, my patient hid under her bed,

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:03.200
but after I coaxed her out, she didn't mind her bath at all.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:09.600
[Narrator:] The student nurses learn here to give tender, considerate care.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:14.160
They keep charts for their patients as the 
registered nurses do.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.520
They prepare formulas.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.840
They confer with the dietitian.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.840
They help in preparing for surgery.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.120
Rose Gomez here is making up the surgical bed.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:27.400
They get the supplies necessary for the 
operations.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:31.120
They observe in the operating room amphitheater 
during surgery.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.920
Sometimes they assist at the scrub table.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:40.160
The crowded waiting room on clinic days keeps them busy as they assist doctors and nurses,

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:44.200
acting as interpreters sometimes when there is a language difficulty.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.040
Taking a patient's history.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:49.840
Explaining about medicines and doctor's 
directions.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:54.360
Practical nurse students also learn to assist the public health nurses,

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.200
making home visits on the Navajo reservation.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:02.480
They assist in treating patients and demonstrating 
proper baby care.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:08.760
They show how to bathe a baby with oil instead of 
the precious water so scarce on the reservation.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:14.920
In visits to these widely scattered hogans on the 
vast reservation, which little Ms. Gumbai could not

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:21.400
even imagine short months ago, the practical nurse student comes to know its people...

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.240
its summer aspects,

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.400
its winter face.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:45.320
Students also assist public health nurses in Indian health clinics at the pueblos.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:53.080
Here Laverna High Hawk aids public health nurse Tua at Santa Ana, talking with patient Joe Garcia.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:57.280
She confers with the mothers and helps weigh the 
baby.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.440
Student days are full.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:00.760
They go fast.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.440
Four months of classwork.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:05.000
Seven months' practical experience.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:10.280
Now nearly time for graduation, the girls go back to the Albuquerque school

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.480
for a final review of studies.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:18.640
Teachers make their final reports and evaluations, 
consideration for each girl's record.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:23.640
There are state board examinations to take to 
secure their license to practice.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:26.920
There are happy jokes.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:31.040
Graduation invitations to send proudly home to 
parents.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:37.040
Graduation uniforms to admire, and finally the 
great day.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:40.080
[Speaker 4:] Graduation day.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.280
We are different today.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:46.080
When I came, I wouldn't have thought anything could be finer than our pink uniforms,

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.440
but oh, the whites!

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:53.200
[Narrator:] The whites, symbolic of all they have 
been waiting and working for.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:57.680
Families gather from near and far.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:59.880
Grandmother Maria.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:08.520
The chief nurse officer of the United States Public 
Health Service arrives to address the girls.

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:12.480
The chief nurse of the Indian Health Service is 
there from Washington.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:15.640
The doctors come also to wish them well.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.640
Outside the auditorium the crowd grows.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:26.360
Mothers and fathers, brothers and sisters from 
Dakota, Colorado, Arizona, Oklahoma, Minnesota.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:32.960
Inside, the Indian school band tunes up, and suddenly it's time.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:38.440
In double line they march across the familiar campus to the auditorium

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.360
where the exercises will be held.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:15:25.760
[Music]

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.400
The chief nurse officer tells them...

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:37.200
[Chief Nurse:] I pray for each of you the reward of deep satisfaction which comes only to a nurse:

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:44.760
the satisfaction of a child healed, a troubled spirit 
comforted, a death rate lowered,

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.920
a new way of health succeeding.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:52.400
[Narrator:] And as they listen, they're thinking big 
thoughts.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:54.720
[Laverna Cucka:] This is an important day.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:58.680
I am excited about it and what is coming.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.800
[Harriet St. Clair:] I wonder who my first patient will 
be.

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.800
[Elsie Curlee:] It didn't seem possible that today 
would ever come.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:08.240
My, I feel so proud.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:10.160
I know my mother is, too.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:13.960
[Narrator:] Miss Cucka rises to give the class response.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:23.440
[Laverna Cucka:] During our year at the Indian School of Practical Nursing,

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:26.560
we have had the opportunity to learn our chosen profession.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:32.320
For many of us it has been a lifelong desire, for we know that as a licensed practical nurse,

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:37.000
we can serve our Indian people and assist in improving their health.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:46.120
[Narrator:] There are certificates and pins and 
congratulations.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:50.760
And then they are graduates, and tomorrow is 
ahead.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:56.480
They are eligible to serve as graduate licensed practical nurses in any state in the union

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:58.120
and in any hospital.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:03.880
Many will serve by choice in Indian hospitals or field assignments throughout the West,

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:10.920
to help add health and knowledge of the gentle art of healing to the other arts and treasures of their people.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:16.280
But even as these graduates leave, a new class is 
coming in.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:23.260
Would you like to join them?

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.440
This is your invitation.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:35.060
[Music]

